{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34090-requiem-directory-updated","id":34090,"title":"Requiem Directory Updated","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-20T14:47:18-08:00","id":34090,"title":"Requiem Directory Updated","content":"Took a while, but the Requiem Genre Directory (Tabletop version) has been updated with the core rules update from &quot;Blood &amp; Smoke&quot;. As with the God-Machine rules update, old items that have been changed in the new version are indicated in blue; old items no that are effectively removed in the new version are indicated in red italics. Please note that some of this is a case of &quot;best guess&quot;... and in all cases, it's up to your particular table or troupe or club to figure out what if any of this is in use.<br /> <br /> As always, the full run of genre directories are here: <a href=\"http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","user":"Jessilaurn","date":". 12-20-2013, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T14:55:45-08:00","id":34097,"title":"","content":"Wow, those are extremely useful guides. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T13:37:09-08:00","id":34587,"title":"","content":"Very useful. Thanks. A question, have been the Shadow Cults eliminated in B&amp;S?, because your directory counts them as eliminated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T13:50:52-08:00","id":34593,"title":"","content":"A shadow cult is basically a Mystery Cult. They haven't been Eliminated, they've been more renamed and given a framework to make your own. They aren't a corebook concept regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T21:00:19-08:00","id":34763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34090-requiem-directory-updated?p=34587#post34587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very useful. Thanks. A question, have been the Shadow Cults eliminated in B&amp;S?, because your directory counts them as eliminated</div> </div> </div> </div>They still exist. They're just not mentioned in the limited space we had in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T06:27:38-08:00","id":35534,"title":"","content":"Ayup. That's one of those things that fell into &quot;best guess&quot;. The mechanics for the Shadow Cult Initiation Meri and the like from the Mekhet clanbook seemed very much superseded by those for the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit - which basically opens the entire cult thing up to everyone - and as such I made a &quot;best guess&quot; and red-texted the former in favour of the latter. As with pretty much anything, it's up to a given group to decide what's actually in play and what isn't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, remember this. These directories that I do aren't an official product. They aren't an official line, let alone a hard-and-fast official line. They're just something I do out of a desire to have complete indices for the World of Darkness, and that I share with the broader community. And even now, some seven years after putting up the first one for Requiem, I still find little things that need correcting. If you happen to notice something that does need fixing, please do flag me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#a7cdc2d4d4cecbc6d2d5c9e7c0cac6cecb89c4c8ca\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"4e242b3d3d27222f3b3c200e29232f2722602d2123\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> so I can get it fixed.<br /> <br /> Finally, I do want to eventually put together complete directories for the OWoD genres as well. But unlike NWoD, I don't own all of the OWoD products, which means I have to rely on &quot;data-miners&quot; to help me out there (unlike NWoD, where I do my own mining)... and willing-and-able data-miners have been vanishingly few. If someone (1) really wants those guides to happen and (2) is willing and able, please shoot me a note at the above e-mail address and we'll talk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","user":"Jessilaurn","date":". 12-23-2013, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T07:27:31-08:00","id":35563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessilaurn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34090-requiem-directory-updated?p=35534#post35534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ayup. That's one of those things that fell into &quot;best guess&quot;. The mechanics for the Shadow Cult Initiation Meri and the like from the Mekhet clanbook seemed very much superseded by those for the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit - which basically opens the entire cult thing up to everyone - and as such I made a &quot;best guess&quot; and red-texted the former in favour of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if you're just talking about mechanics, then yes, Shadow Cult Initiation would probably be a customized version of Mystery Cult Initiation. I was saying that the organizations themselves still exist.<br /> <br /> Nice guides, by the way. I should have said that earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T09:35:37-08:00","id":35633,"title":"","content":"Thanks Rose; they're a labor of love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - Jess<br /> <br /> (Edit: reverted the specific Shadow Cult listing back to black text. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","user":"Jessilaurn","date":". 12-23-2013, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:31:42-07:00","id":860454,"title":"","content":"Bit of an update. I've been in a spate of updating of various things, and one of the results is that the Requiem directory has been split out into a 1st Ed directory and a 2nd Ed directory. They, along with all the others, can be found here: <a href=\"http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}